    "summary": "Restored snapshot 037c658 (git diff --stat vs refs/workflow/ab4108408f3548e5/intel printed nothing; only owned paths). step.ts: added the pure freeCoverage(config, state, view, playerId, type) over an internal coveredFree used in phase 2 of the step (delivery 'covered', nothing sent, answered covered by answerRequests) and in targetedRumorAvailability (now may return 'covered'); (a) carrier-only type once tick >= carrierRevealTick, (b) carrier-only type in the pending set after gather; eligibility is planLead's. At a boundary a pending type with an active journal rumor is dropped without a no-lead. Tests: start-step cover (control start + late joiner), decideLeads with/without starting, all-orders free-trigger tie-break, multi-request none group, @ts-expect-error on CarrierSighting.reason and on a carrier-sighting body, four free-coverage scenarios with availability/freeCoverage agreement. Property checker: checkCharges keeps every lead per (player,type), and checks free coverage independently from the view; EXERCISED adds covered:broadcast and covered:pending. Changed expectations: 'defer a capped free sighting...' (sun-buy capped->covered), 'deliver two pending types together...' (sun-buy capped->covered), 'lift the sighting cap from the carrier reveal on' (rewritten: the cap lift is shown by two free sightings in one snapshot; purchases are covered). 27 typecheck-clean one-line mutations were applied on a scratch copy; each broke a named test (M20 breaks npm run typecheck via TS2578); list is in docs/intel.md 'Tests per branch'. Ran: npm ci, npm run typecheck, npm run test:unit (603 pass), npm run test:integration (36 pass), npm run build (smoke passed).",
